      "content": "Melanoma on darker skin often appears showerlike or flat lesions on palms, soles, or nail beds rather than the classic irregular borders seen on lighter skin. It may also present as a new dark spot on existing nevi or as a changing streak under the nail, which can be more difficult to detect. Remember that while ABCDE (Asymmetry, Border, Color, Diameter, Evolution) is still useful, focus heavily on \"new pigmented spots\" and lesions that evolve in people with darker sun-protected skin. Consistently reviewing these subtle presentations is key to early detection on your boards.",
